A||||6||Cheever2||A typical drive to work||||6||
Z||000000||Cheever2||03-13-2001||07:02 PM||||I get on the highway coming to work.  Soon the traffic opens up so I can easily go the 70 mph speed limit.  Glancing up I say "Thank you!"  'Bout that time I notice in the rearview a black Volvo that came from nowhere.  He has no clear lane to move into, so I figure why not move on up and give him room to pass.  I do, but he seems content to stay with me.  Fine.  I'm curious to know just how fast he wants to go so I push it a little, but soon at 90 mph we catch up to the next bunch of slower cars.  This is when he chooses the far left lane and is able to move ahead of me.  Cool, good for him, have a nice day sir.  Doesn't take me long to see he made the right choice so I move over there too, behind him now, but not close because he's up to at least 100.  He starts moving to the right lanes, possibly in preparation for the next exit.  You know how quickly the traffic changes?  Well it opened up ahead of me, but closed up ahead of him.  I fly by, don't have time to get a good look at him clenching his teeth, but I know he's doing it.  Sorry, pal, some days are better than others.<P>So after my exit and down the street a little, I'm in stop-n-go traffic just a block from my last turn and in the rearview I do a doubletake on a Lexus SC300, remembering that video someone posted showing one blowing by a Viper & a couple of RX-7's.  I'm in the right lane, he moves beside me, we wait through another red light.  He's a few feet ahead, so I'm getting a good look, yep, just like the one in that video (wasn't that taken in Texas?).  Well, the light changes, the cars ahead start moving, but he's holding back like he wants me to get back even with him.  I'm just happy he noticed my car, but I AM a realist, I'm not stupid.  So I get what I can in first gear and he gets what he can before catching up to traffic in about 1.5 seconds, but almost as soon as I was off the clutch I'm at my turn and just let him go, probably laughing his butt off thinking "This guy actually thinks he has a chance?".  But now, see, he has to go through life wondering, with that little hesitant voice saying "Could he really have taken me?".  Meanwhile I'm going through life with the attitude "Do ya feel lucky, punk?".<BR> <P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
